===Etymology===
{{suffix|polyseme|y|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
{{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpɒ.lɪ.siː.mi/|lang=en}}, {{IPAchar|/pə.ˈlɪ.sɪ.mi/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|polysemies}}

# {{lb|en|semantics}} The ability of [[word]]s, [[sign]]s and [[symbol]]s to have [[multiple]] [[meaning]]s.
#: ''[...] '''polysemy''', which is the greedy habit some words have of taking more than one meaning for themselves.'' [[w:Erin McKean|Erin McKean]], [http://www.ted.com/index.php/talks/view/id/161 speech at TED].

